course: dictionary
lesson: 15660
title: Thinned: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «thinned» is one of them. To choose the right meaning, look at the words around it. Ask yourself: what is getting less?
explain: «She thinned the paint with water.» Water makes paint less thick, so thinned means made thinner. «The crowd thinned as the rain started.» Now fewer people are standing together, so thinned means less crowded.
explain: Gardeners use thinned too. «Mum thinned the seedlings so the strong ones could grow.» Some young plants were pulled out to give the others room. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Thinned is the past form of the verb thin: thin, thins, thinned, thinning.
fact: «Thinned» can also be an adjective, as in «a thinned sauce».
fact: «Thinned» means made thinner or less thick, as in «She thinned the paint with water».
fact: «Thinned» can mean less crowded or less dense, as in «The crowd thinned out».
fact: In gardening, «thinned» means took out some young plants so the others have room to grow. For hair, «thinned» means became thinner, with less hair.
exercise: «She thinned the paint with water.» What does thinned mean here? | Mixed with sugar | Painted a much bigger picture | Made louder | *Made thinner or less thick
exercise: «The crowd thinned out after the match.» What does thinned mean here? | Became hotter | Grew taller | *Became less crowded | Became more noisy
exercise: Gardeners thinned the seedlings. What did they do? | Watered every plant twice | Planted more seeds in the same spot | Painted the plant pots | *Took out some young plants so the others had room
test: «His hair thinned as he got older.» What does thinned mean here? | Turned bright red | Was washed and dried | Grew longer and curlier | *Became thinner, with less hair
test: «The sauce was thinned with stock.» Which word means the same as thinned here? | *Made less thick | Heated | Sweetened | Covered
exam: Which sentence uses thinned to mean less crowded? | «His hair thinned as he got older.» | *«The crowd thinned as the shops closed.» | «The lake was deep and still.» | «She thinned the paint with water.»
